35,2,1,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, four to nine minutes every morning? That’s huge! Plus, shuffles last two whole weeks! My gaps are gone!","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, time is a symptom. The billing is the root. We pay for empty desks, and every move costs 6,200 yen. We need a layout that stops the bleeding.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@Toshio, the survey confirms daylight is the top complaint. The plan gives four desks windows, leaving three in the dark. That imbalance is unacceptable.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"@Mizuki, daylight is a preference. My data shows the printer row is nine decibels louder. I need a spot that protects my body, not just my eyes.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Mizuki, three desks in the dark? That’s tough! @Shion, I hope the printer noise isn’t too loud for you. I’m worried about how we all fit together!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Shion, nine decibels is loud! But @Toshio, two weeks of shuffling is a disaster! I need a layout that stops the chaos before it starts!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, two weeks of chaos is a 6,200 yen penalty per desk. We must design a layout that is final, or the budget line collapses.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shion, nine decibels is a real burden. But the survey shows daylight is the primary pain point. We must address both, not just one.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Mizuki, daylight is a preference. My body is the priority. The physio note confirms my setup takes days to settle. I need a stable, quiet spot to protect my posture.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Shion, I’m so sorry your body is hurting! @Toshio, I found that our new joiners learned by overhearing! If we sit apart, they miss out on the team’s real rhythm!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Yumi, overhearing is great! But if we sit too close, I can’t focus! I need a layout that keeps my morning gaps safe!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Yumi, overhearing is inefficient. The 6,200 yen per move means we cannot afford to experiment. We need a static layout that minimizes future re-runs.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Yumi, overhearing is valuable, but it shouldn’t come at the cost of the three stuck in the dark. We need a layout that balances access fairly, not just convenience.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Yumi, overhearing is inefficient. My body needs stability. The physio note confirms my setup takes days to settle. I need a quiet, fixed spot to protect my posture.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
